As volume charge density is $\rho$, then in terms of charge density, $\begin{aligned}$E &amp; =$\frac{\rho r}{3 \varepsilon_0}$\\
\quad \quad \quad \rho &amp; =$\frac{3 E \varepsilon_0}{r}
\end{aligned}$Now, electric field, $E=-\frac{d V}{d r}$
Here, $V=A r^2+B\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore$&amp; E=-$\frac{d V}{d r}=-$2 A r+0=-2 A r \\
\therefore &amp; \rho=$\frac{3 E \varepsilon_0}{r}
\end{array} =\frac{3\left(-2 A r \cdot \varepsilon_0\right)}{r}=-$6 A \varepsilon_0
